IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `whs-claims-rules`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- the claimant's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the individual the law is applied to, asking as that person: the worker, prospective worker or other person
-- punished, pressured or misled for a safety reason (Part 6); the injured worker or a family member who wants a
-- prosecution brought (ss 231, 232); the worker affected by an inspector's or Comcare's decision (Part 12); the person
-- whose property an inspector damaged or seized (s 184); the worker with a contract term or a charge about safety
-- (ss 267, 272, 273). Every rule is in whs-claims-rules.l4; this module asks, and restates none.
--
-- The Commonwealth Act covers work for the Commonwealth, its public authorities and non-Commonwealth licensees
-- (s 12, encoded in ../baseline-2026-10/whs-worker.l4); work under a State or Territory WHS law is not covered here.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Work Health and Safety Act 2011 -- a claimant's questions`

§§ `Part 6 -- if I was punished, pressured or misled for a safety reason` -- arises only if something was done to the person

@export Is what was done to me "discriminatory conduct" under s 105 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth)? It covers dismissal, ending a contract for services, detriment, altering my position, not engaging me or offering me worse terms, and ending or refusing a commercial arrangement, and organising or threatening any of these.
GIVEN `what they did` IS A `What they did` @desc What the other person did, or organised, or threatened to do, to you. Choose "none of these" if none fits.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is what was done to me discriminatory conduct?` `what they did` MEANS
    `s 105 -- it is discriminatory conduct` `what they did`

@export Was it done to me for a "prohibited reason" under s 106 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth): because of my safety role, my use of a power or function under the Act, helping an inspector, raising a safety issue with someone the Act lists, or seeking compliance?
GIVEN `why they did it` IS A `Why they did it` @desc The reason you say it was done. Choose "another reason" if none fits.
      `whom I raised it with` IS A `Whom I raised it with` @desc If the reason is that you raised a safety issue or concern: with whom you raised it, or proposed to. Otherwise choose "I did not raise an issue".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was it done for a prohibited reason?` `why they did it` `whom I raised it with` MEANS
    `s 106 -- it was for a prohibited reason` `why they did it` `whom I raised it with`

@export Was I coerced or induced in a way s 108 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth) prohibits: action taken or threatened against me (or withheld) to make me use or not use a power or function under the Act, or give up a safety role?
GIVEN `they acted against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they take or organise action against you, or threaten to, or not take (or threaten not to take) an action in relation to you?
      `they meant to make me do it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they do it intending to coerce or induce you, or a third person?
      `what they tried to make me do` IS A `What they tried to make me do` @desc What they were trying to make you, or the third person, do or not do.
      `an emergency direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it a reasonable direction given by an emergency services worker in an emergency?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I coerced or induced?` `they acted against me` `they meant to make me do it` `what they tried to make me do` `an emergency direction` MEANS
    `s 108 -- it was prohibited coercion or inducement` `they acted against me` `they meant to make me do it` `what they tried to make me do` `an emergency direction`

@export Was I misled in a way s 109 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth) prohibits: a false or misleading statement, made knowingly or recklessly, about my rights or obligations under the Act, my ability to start or join a process under it, or to complain to someone who enforces it?
GIVEN `it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what you were told false or misleading?
      `they knew or were reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person who told you know it was false or misleading, or were they reckless about it?
      `what I was misled about` IS A `What I was misled about` @desc What the statement was about.
      `I would be expected to rely on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would someone in your position be expected to rely on it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I misled about my rights?` `it was false or misleading` `they knew or were reckless` `what I was misled about` `I would be expected to rely on it` MEANS
    `s 109 -- it was prohibited misrepresentation` `it was false or misleading` `they knew or were reckless` `what I was misled about` `I would be expected to rely on it`

@export Can I start a court proceeding under s 112 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth) over discriminatory conduct or coercion, on the day I would start it? Checks what I complain of, whether I may apply, the 1-year limit (s 113(1)) and the bars on other claims (s 115(a), (c)).
GIVEN `what I complain of` IS A `What I complain of` @desc What was done to you: discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason, coercion or inducement under s 108, a misrepresentation under s 109, or nothing Part 6 prohibits.
      `who I am in the claim` IS A `Who I am in the claim` @desc Whether you are the person affected, a representative that person authorised, or someone else.
      `the day I knew, or ought to have known` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew, or ought to have known, that you had a claim (usually the day of the dismissal or other conduct). ISO date, e.g. 2026-03-15.
      `the day I would start` IS A DATE @desc The day you would file the application in court. ISO date.
      `I have another live claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you started a proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under another Commonwealth or State law (for example a Fair Work general protections claim) and not withdrawn it?
      `I lost another claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you failed in a proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under another Commonwealth or State law, other than a workers' compensation claim?
GIVETH A `Can I start a s 112 proceeding`
`Can I start a court proceeding?` `what I complain of` `who I am in the claim` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` `the day I would start` `I have another live claim` `I lost another claim` MEANS
    `ss 112, 113(1), 115(a), (c) -- whether I can start` `what I complain of` `who I am in the claim` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` `the day I would start` `I have another live claim` `I lost another claim`

@export By what day must I start a court proceeding under s 112 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth)? Not more than 1 year after the day I knew or ought to have known I had a claim (s 113(1)).
GIVEN `the day I knew, or ought to have known` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew, or ought to have known, that you had a claim. ISO date, e.g. 2026-03-15.
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I start?` `the day I knew, or ought to have known` MEANS
    `s 113(1) -- the last day to start` `the day I knew, or ought to have known`

@export What orders can the court make for me under s 112 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth)? An injunction, compensation, reinstatement or re-employment, or another order, depending on what was done, who did it, the presumption and defence in s 113, and other compensation or orders. An empty list means none.
GIVEN `what I complain of` IS A `What I complain of` @desc What was done to you.
      `their part in it` IS A `Their part in it` @desc Whether the person you would sue did it themselves, or requested, instructed, induced, encouraged, authorised or assisted another person to do it. Ignored for coercion.
      `they proved it was not a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other side proved, on the balance of probabilities, that the safety reason was not a substantial reason for what they did? (It is presumed to be one until they do, s 113(2).)
      `they proved the reasonable-compliance defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other side proved that what they did was reasonable in the circumstances and that a substantial reason for it was to comply with a WHS law (s 113(3))?
      `I am or was an employee or applied to be one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, or are you, their employee, or did you apply to be employed by them?
      `a court already made a s 111 order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court, on convicting them of an offence under s 104 or 107 for the same conduct, already ordered compensation or reinstatement for you (s 111)?
      `I already got compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received compensation for the matter under another Commonwealth or State law?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order`
`What orders can the court make for me?` `what I complain of` `their part in it` `they proved it was not a substantial reason` `they proved the reasonable-compliance defence` `I am or was an employee or applied to be one` `a court already made a s 111 order` `I already got compensation` MEANS
    `s 112(3) -- the orders the court may make` `what I complain of` `their part in it` `they proved it was not a substantial reason` `they proved the reasonable-compliance defence` `I am or was an employee or applied to be one` `a court already made a s 111 order` `I already got compensation`

@export If the person who discriminated against me is convicted under s 104 or 107 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth), what orders can the court make for me (s 111)? Compensation, and for an employee or job applicant reinstatement or employment; none if a court already made a s 112 order about the same conduct (s 114(2)).
GIVEN `they were convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been convicted or found guilty of an offence under s 104 (discriminatory conduct) or s 107 (requesting or helping it)?
      `I am or was an employee or applied to be one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, or are you, their employee, or did you apply to be employed by them?
      `a court already made a s 112 order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court already made an order under s 112 for you about the same conduct?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order`
`What orders can a criminal court make for me?` `they were convicted` `I am or was an employee or applied to be one` `a court already made a s 112 order` MEANS
    `s 111 -- the orders open on conviction` `they were convicted` `I am or was an employee or applied to be one` `a court already made a s 112 order`

@export Are the elements of the s 104 offence made out against the person who discriminated against me (Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? The conduct, for a prohibited reason, done intentionally, with the safety reason the dominant reason; that is presumed once the prosecution makes its s 110(1) case, unless they prove otherwise (ss 104, 110).
GIVEN `it was discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was what was done discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason (ss 105, 106)?
      `they meant to do it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the accused intend to engage in the conduct (the fault element, s 104(3))?
      `the prosecution made its s 110(1) case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the prosecution proved the conduct and the s 106 circumstance (for example, that you raised a safety issue), and adduced evidence that the conduct was for that reason?
      `they proved it was not the dominant reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: has the accused proved, on the balance of probabilities, that the safety reason was not the dominant reason? Otherwise any value; it is ignored.
      `the prosecution proved it was the dominant reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the prosecution did not make its s 110(1) case: has it proved that the safety reason was the dominant reason? Otherwise any value; it is ignored.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can they be convicted for discriminating against me?` `it was discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `they meant to do it` `the prosecution made its s 110(1) case` `they proved it was not the dominant reason` `the prosecution proved it was the dominant reason` MEANS
    `ss 104, 110 -- the elements of the offence are made out` `it was discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason` `they meant to do it` `the prosecution made its s 110(1) case` `they proved it was not the dominant reason` `the prosecution proved it was the dominant reason`

@export What is the most the person who discriminated against me, coerced me or misled me can be fined for the offence under s 104, 107, 108 or 109 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth)? The tier A monetary penalty, as printed in Schedule 4 before annual indexation.
GIVEN `they are a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who did it a body corporate (a company), rather than an individual?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most they can be fined for it?` `they are a company` MEANS
    `Schedule 4 cl 2 -- the tier A monetary penalty` `they are a company`

§§ `Part 13 -- if I want them prosecuted` -- arises only after a death, serious injury or dangerous incident

@export May I ask Comcare in writing to bring a prosecution, on the day I would ask (s 231 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? Only for industrial manslaughter or a Category 1 or 2 offence, when none has been brought, and only 6 to 18 months after it happened, or within 6 months after a coronial report or inquest.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The offence I consider was committed` @desc The offence you consider was committed.
      `I reasonably consider it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you reasonably consider that the offence was committed?
      `a prosecution has been brought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a prosecution for the offence already been brought?
      `what I base it on` IS A `What I base it on` @desc Whether you base it on what happened, or on a coronial report, inquiry or inquest.
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day it happened, or the day the coronial report was made or the inquiry or inquest ended. ISO date.
      `the day I would ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you would make the written request. ISO date.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`May I ask for a prosecution?` `the offence` `I reasonably consider it` `a prosecution has been brought` `what I base it on` `the day` `the day I would ask` MEANS
    `s 231(1), (1A), (1B) -- I may ask` `the offence` `I reasonably consider it` `a prosecution has been brought` `what I base it on` `the day` `the day I would ask`

@export Between which days may I ask Comcare to bring a prosecution (s 231(1B) of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))?
GIVEN `what I base it on` IS A `What I base it on` @desc Whether you base it on what happened, or on a coronial report, inquiry or inquest.
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day it happened, or the day the coronial report was made or the inquiry or inquest ended. ISO date.
GIVETH A `Request window`
`Between which days may I ask?` `what I base it on` `the day` MEANS
    `s 231(1B) -- the window` `what I base it on` `the day`

@export By what day must Comcare answer my written request for a prosecution (s 231(2) of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? Within 3 months after it receives it.
GIVEN `the day Comcare received it` IS A DATE @desc The day Comcare received your request. ISO date.
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must Comcare answer me?` `the day Comcare received it` MEANS
    `s 231(2) -- the last day for the advice` `the day Comcare received it`

@export Is Comcare late in answering my written request for a prosecution (s 231(2) of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth)), as at a day?
GIVEN `the day Comcare received it` IS A DATE @desc The day Comcare received your request. ISO date.
      `it has answered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has Comcare told you in writing whether the investigation is complete (and, if so, whether a prosecution will be brought)?
      `the day it answered` IS A DATE @desc If it has answered, the day it did. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, usually today. ISO date.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is Comcare late in answering me?` `the day Comcare received it` `it has answered` `the day it answered` `the day asked about` MEANS
    NOT (`s 231(2) -- the duty was kept, or can still be` `the day Comcare received it` `it has answered` `the day it answered` `the day asked about`)

@export By what day must Comcare refer my matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions, after it said no prosecution will be brought and I asked in writing for a referral (s 231(3)(b) of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? No answer if either has not happened.
GIVEN `Comcare said no prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has Comcare told you that a prosecution for industrial manslaughter or a Category 1 or 2 offence will not be brought?
      `I asked for a referral` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you asked Comcare in writing to refer the matter to the Director of Public Prosecutions?
      `the day I asked` IS A DATE @desc The day you asked for the referral. ISO date.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By what day must Comcare refer my matter?` `Comcare said no prosecution` `I asked for a referral` `the day I asked` MEANS
    `s 231(3)(b) -- the last day to refer` `Comcare said no prosecution` `I asked for a referral` `the day I asked`

@export Until when can the person responsible be prosecuted for the offence (s 232 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? The latest of 2 years after Comcare learns of it, 1 year after a coronial report or inquiry that shows an offence, and 6 months after a WHS undertaking is breached or withdrawn; industrial manslaughter at any time.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `The offence I consider was committed` @desc The offence.
      `the day Comcare learned of it` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence first came to Comcare's notice. ISO date.
      `an inquiry showed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a coronial report, coronial inquiry or inquest, or an official inquiry (such as a Royal Commission) make it appear that an offence was committed?
      `the day the inquiry ended` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the report was made or the inquiry or inquest ended. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `an undertaking was breached or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a WHS undertaking given about the offence, and then breached, or withdrawn with Comcare's agreement?
      `the undertaking day` IS A DATE @desc If so, the latest of the day it was breached, the day Comcare learned of the breach, and the day Comcare agreed to its withdrawal. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `the court accepts fresh evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a Category 1 offence: has fresh evidence been found that the court is satisfied could not reasonably have been found in time?
GIVETH A `Time to prosecute`
`Until when can they be prosecuted?` `the offence` `the day Comcare learned of it` `an inquiry showed an offence` `the day the inquiry ended` `an undertaking was breached or withdrawn` `the undertaking day` `the court accepts fresh evidence` MEANS
    `s 232 -- how long they can be prosecuted` `the offence` `the day Comcare learned of it` `an inquiry showed an offence` `the day the inquiry ended` `an undertaking was breached or withdrawn` `the undertaking day` `the court accepts fresh evidence`

§§ `Part 12 -- if an inspector's or Comcare's decision affects me` -- arises only if a notice or decision was made

@export Can I have this decision reviewed, and where do I go first (ss 223, 224 and 229 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? Internal review by Comcare for an inspector's decision, the Fair Work Commission for Comcare's own.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision you want reviewed.
      `my interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a worker whose interests are affected by the decision?
      `the notice was issued to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice (or provisional improvement notice) issued to you?
      `I am entitled to the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a seized thing: are you the person entitled to it (the person it was seized from, or its owner if that person may not possess it)?
      `I am an HSR for an affected worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a health and safety representative who represents a worker whose interests are affected?
      `I am an HSR whose own interests are affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a health and safety representative whose own interests are affected by the decision (for example, the representative whose training it concerns)?
      `I am an affected worker's s 52(1)(b) representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a decision on failed work group negotiations: are you the representative an affected worker appointed for the negotiations (s 52(1)(b))?
GIVETH A `Where to go`
`Can I have the decision reviewed?` `the decision` `my interests are affected` `the notice was issued to me` `I am entitled to the thing` `I am an HSR for an affected worker` `I am an HSR whose own interests are affected` `I am an affected worker's s 52(1)(b) representative` MEANS
    `ss 223, 224, 229 -- where to go` `the decision` (`My standing` WITH
        `I am a worker whose interests are affected` IS `my interests are affected`
        `I am the person to whom the notice was issued` IS `the notice was issued to me`
        `I am the person entitled to the seized thing` IS `I am entitled to the thing`
        `I am a health and safety representative for an affected worker` IS `I am an HSR for an affected worker`
        `I am a health and safety representative whose own interests are affected` IS `I am an HSR whose own interests are affected`
        `I am the representative of an affected worker appointed for the purpose of s 52(1)(b)` IS `I am an affected worker's s 52(1)(b) representative`)

@export By what day must I apply to Comcare for internal review of an inspector's decision (s 224 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? 14 days after it came to my notice, or for an improvement notice the shorter of that and its compliance period. Comcare may allow longer.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision you want reviewed.
      `the day it came to my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision first came to your notice. ISO date.
      `the day the notice was issued` IS A DATE @desc For an improvement notice: the day it was issued. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `the compliance day` IS A DATE @desc For an improvement notice: the day stated in it by which the contravention must be remedied. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I ask for internal review?` `the decision` `the day it came to my notice` `the day the notice was issued` `the compliance day` MEANS
    `s 224 -- the last day to apply for internal review` `the decision` `the day it came to my notice` `the day the notice was issued` `the compliance day`

@export If the internal reviewer does not decide, on what day is the decision taken to be confirmed (s 226 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? 14 days after my application, paused while I answer a request for information; or the end of my time to answer if I do not.
GIVEN `the day my application was received` IS A DATE @desc The day Comcare received your application for internal review. ISO date.
      `the reviewer asked for information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the reviewer ask you for further information?
      `the day it asked` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it asked. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
      `the days it gave me` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many days it gave you to answer (the Act requires at least 7).
      `I answered in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the information within that time?
      `the day I answered` IS A DATE @desc If you did, the day you gave it. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
GIVETH A DATE
`When is the decision taken to be confirmed?` `the day my application was received` `the reviewer asked for information` `the day it asked` `the days it gave me` `I answered in time` `the day I answered` MEANS
    `s 226 -- the day the decision is taken to be confirmed` `the day my application was received` `the reviewer asked for information` `the day it asked` `the days it gave me` `I answered in time` `the day I answered`

@export Is the decision stayed (put on hold) while my internal review runs (s 228 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? Automatically, except a prohibition or non-disturbance notice, which the reviewer may stay; a stay application not decided in 1 working day is taken to be granted. Comcare's own decisions (forfeiture, return of seized things, varying or cancelling a notice) have no internal review, and s 228 does not answer for them.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision under review.
      `I applied for a stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a prohibition or non-disturbance notice: did you apply for a stay?
      `the reviewer decided in 1 working day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you applied, did the reviewer decide your application within 1 working day after receiving it?
      `the reviewer granted a stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the reviewer grant a stay (on your application or on its own initiative)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the decision on hold during review?` `the decision` `I applied for a stay` `the reviewer decided in 1 working day` `the reviewer granted a stay` MEANS
    `s 228 -- the decision is stayed` `the decision` `I applied for a stay` `the reviewer decided in 1 working day` `the reviewer granted a stay`

@export By what day must I apply to the Fair Work Commission for external review (s 229(2) of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? 28 days for a forfeiture, 14 days for any other decision, after it came to my notice; or 14 days after reasons the Commission required Comcare to give me.
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc The decision you want reviewed (for a decision on internal review, the original decision).
      `the day it came to my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision (or the internal review decision) first came to your notice. ISO date.
      `the Commission required reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Fair Work Commission require Comcare to give you a statement of reasons?
      `the day I got the reasons` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day the statement was given to you. Otherwise any date; it is ignored.
GIVETH A DATE
`By what day must I go to the Fair Work Commission?` `the decision` `the day it came to my notice` `the Commission required reasons` `the day I got the reasons` MEANS
    `s 229(2) -- the last day to apply to the Fair Work Commission` `the decision` `the day it came to my notice` `the Commission required reasons` `the day I got the reasons`

§§ `Part 9 -- if an inspector's powers cost me` -- arises only if an inspector entered, searched or seized

@export May I claim compensation from the Commonwealth for loss or expense caused by an inspector's entry, search, seizure or other power under ss 163 to 181 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth) (s 184)? A court orders it only if satisfied it is just.
GIVEN `I had loss or expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you incur loss or expense?
      `it was caused by an inspector's entry powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it because of an inspector's use (or purported use) of a power on entering a workplace, under a search warrant, or to seize things (ss 163 to 181)?
      `the court finds it just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that it is just to order compensation in your case? Answer yes to ask only whether you may claim.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I get compensation for what an inspector did?` `I had loss or expense` `it was caused by an inspector's entry powers` `the court finds it just` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 184(1) -- I may claim` `I had loss or expense` `it was caused by an inspector's entry powers`
    WHEN JUST `may claim` THEN `s 184(3) -- the court may order it` `may claim` `the court finds it just`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `Civil claims, contract terms and charges (ss 267, 272, 273)`

@export Does the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth) itself give me a right to sue in a civil court for this (s 267)? Only for discriminatory or coercive conduct under Part 6; an injury claim lies in negligence or workers' compensation, which the Act leaves unaffected.
GIVEN `my claim is about` IS A `My civil claim is about` @desc What your civil claim would be about.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the Act give me a right to sue?` `my claim is about` MEANS
    `s 267 -- the Act gives me a right of action` `my claim is about`

@export Is a term of my contract or agreement void because it takes away or shifts a duty under the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth) (s 272)?
GIVEN `it excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to exclude, limit or modify how the Act applies, or any duty owed under it?
      `it transfers a duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term purport to transfer to another person a duty owed under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the contract term void?` `it excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty` `it transfers a duty` MEANS
    `s 272 -- the term is void` `it excludes, limits or modifies the Act or a duty` `it transfers a duty`

@export Did the business break s 273 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth) by charging me for safety? A business must not impose, or permit, a levy or charge on a worker for anything done or provided for work health and safety (such as protective equipment or training).
GIVEN `I was charged for something done or provided for safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the business you work for impose, or let someone impose, a levy or charge on you for anything done or provided in relation to work health and safety?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Did the business break the rule against charging me for safety?` `I was charged for something done or provided for safety` MEANS
    NOT (`s 273 -- the prohibition was kept` `I was charged for something done or provided for safety`)

@export What is the most the business can be fined for charging me for safety (s 273 of the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (Cth))? The tier F monetary penalty, as printed in Schedule 4 before annual indexation.
GIVEN `the business is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business a body corporate (a company), rather than an individual?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most the business can be fined for charging me?` `the business is a company` MEANS
    `Schedule 4 cl 2 -- the tier F monetary penalty` `the business is a company`
